### 1. Test Public Route (Only global middleware runs)
GET http://localhost:5001/api/public

###

### 2. Test Protected Route without Authorization (Blocked by requireAuth middleware)
GET http://localhost:5001/api/protected

###

### 3. Test Protected Route with Authorization (Passes requireAuth middleware)
GET http://localhost:5001/api/protected
Authorization: Bearer secret-token

###

### 4. Test Admin Route with Authorization (Chained middlewares: requireAuth -> validateAdmin)
GET http://localhost:5001/api/admin
Authorization: Bearer secret-token

###

### 5. Test Admin Route with wrong role (This would need modification in middleware to test, but token passes the first step)
# Since the hardcoded token assigns 'admin' role, this will successfully pass both middlewares.
GET http://localhost:5001/api/admin
Authorization: Bearer secret-token
